      <Comment source="xu, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: Phycocyanobilins Phycocyanobilin| is a blue pigment that belongs to the |FRAME: Phycobilins phycobilins|. It is found in |FRAME: TAX-1117| and in the chloroplasts of |FRAME: TAX-2763 rhodophytes|, |FRAME: TAX-38254 glaucocystophytes|, and some |FRAME: TAX-3027 cryptomonads|. |FRAME: Phycocyanobilins Phycocyanobilin| is covalently linked to the |FRAME: Phycobiliproteins phycobiliproteins| |FRAME: Allophycocyanins allophycocyanin|, |FRAME: Phycocyanins phycocyanin|, and |FRAME: Phycoerythrocyanins phycoerythrocyanin| by a thioether bond to conserved cysteine resudues.</Comment>
